MIT License (see the bottom of this file). Code: <a href="https://github.com/MarkAugie/augielab">github.com/MarkAugie/augielab</a></p>
</div>

<template id="explain">
  <h2>What's happening?</h2>
  <h3>Your phone is a stopwatch</h3>
  <p>Each GPS satellite broadcasts the exact time from its atomic clock. Your receiver notes when each signal arrives, and since radio travels at the speed of light, the delay gives the distance to that satellite. A billionth of a second of error is 30 cm. Your phone's clock is cheap quartz, nowhere near good enough, so the receiver treats its own clock error as a fourth unknown and solves for it along with east, north and height. That's why it needs at least four satellites. Remember this; it matters for the Einstein part.</p>
  <h3>Why the dot wanders</h3>
  <p>The signal is slowed a little by the ionosphere and the weather, the satellites' broadcast orbits and clocks are off by a bit, and signals bounce off buildings and trees. Nobody adds these errors on purpose; that stopped in May 2000. Under open sky, GPS.gov says smartphones are typically within about 4.9 m (16 ft). Notice that the dot doesn't jump around at random: it slowly wanders, because these errors change over a minute or more. Speed it up to see the wander.</p>
  <h3>How surveyors get a centimeter: RTK</h3>
  <p><strong>Real-Time Kinematic</strong> uses a <strong>base station</strong> set up over a point whose position is already known. It sees almost the same errors as your rover a few kilometers away, so it radios corrections every second. RTK also measures the radio wave itself (the carrier, about 19 cm per wave on L1), not just the timing code. Once the receiver has counted the whole waves (getting a "fix", usually in seconds), a typical spec is <strong>8 mm + 1 ppm</strong> horizontal RMS: 1 extra millimeter for every kilometer to the base. The catch is that you need a base, or a subscription to a network of them. Oregon's is ODOT's ORGN.</p>
  <h3>Corrections without a base station</h3>
  <p><strong>Precise Point Positioning</strong> (PPP) skips the base. Instead, precise satellite orbits and clocks, worked out by a worldwide network of tracking stations, are sent to the receiver by satellite or over the internet. Europe's Galileo High Accuracy Service does this free, worldwide, aiming for 20 cm (95%). The trade-off is time: the receiver has to converge, which takes several minutes, rather than fixing in seconds like RTK. Commercial services do better. This is one answer to "real-time corrections without an RTK base station."</p>
  <h3>Einstein and the 38 microseconds</h3>
  <p>A GPS satellite moves at 3.9 km/s, so its clock runs slow by about 7 µs a day (special relativity). It is also 20,200 km up where gravity is weaker, so its clock runs fast by about 45 µs a day (general relativity). Net: <strong>+38 µs a day</strong>. To cancel it, each clock is set before launch to 10.22999999543 MHz instead of 10.23 MHz.</p>
  <h3>The famous "10 km a day" story</h3>
  <p>You'll often read that without that fix, your GPS position would drift about 10 km a day. The clock part is true: 38 µs at the speed of light makes <em>every</em> satellite's range about 11 km too short per day. But every satellite's clock gains the <em>same</em> amount, and your receiver is already solving for a clock error. The shared error just gets added to that, and your position barely moves. GPS World's "Inside the Box" column on GPS and relativity makes this same point. Switch to <strong>Einstein off</strong> and see.</p>
  <h3>So what would break?</h3>
  <p>Two things. First, <strong>the time</strong>. GPS is the world's clock: cell networks, the power grid and stock exchanges sync to it within about a microsecond, and without the fix GPS time would run 38 µs a day fast. Second, the parts that <em>differ</em> from satellite to satellite. Orbits are slightly oval, so each satellite's clock speeds up and slows down twice per orbit, by up to about 45 ns (±15 m of range) for an eccentricity of 0.02. That doesn't cancel, so every receiver corrects it. In the time-lapse, each satellite gets its own random oval orbit, and the satellites are held still in the sky to keep things simple. In real life the ground crew would also notice the clock drift and upload corrections. This page asks what relativity alone would do.</p>
  <h3>The myth switch</h3>
  <p>Set "Receiver solves for its own clock?" to <strong>No</strong> to see how the 10 km story would play out if your receiver had a perfect clock and trusted the satellites completely. All the ranges come up short together, so the solution gets pulled toward the satellites, which are overhead: you end up mostly <em>high in the air</em>, by kilometers a day.</p>
  <h3>Where the randomness comes from</h3>
  <p>Real GPS errors come from the atmosphere and electronics. Here, the random parts of every simulated error come from your browser's random number generator. The original page on augielab.dev can use a quantum random number generator instead.</p>
  <h3>About this page</h3>
  <p>Made by Mark Aughenbaugh for AugieLab. Numbers come from GPS.gov (phones, 4.9 m), typical survey-receiver RTK specs (8 mm + 1 ppm), the Galileo High Accuracy Service target (20 cm, 95%), and GPS World's "Inside the Box" column on GPS and relativity. It's a teaching simulation, not real receiver data.</p>
</template>

<script>
(() => {
  const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);

  // ================= Randomness source =================
  // One switch: leave ENDPOINT empty for demo mode. When the quantum generator is online,
  // set it to a URL that returns {"ok":true,"values":[0..255,...]} for ?n=COUNT (refined, Cicada -p 0).
  const SOURCE = { ENDPOINT: '', NAME: '' };          // classroom edition: always the browser's generator
  let pool = [], fetching = false, quantum = false;
  function setSource(q, fellBack) {
    quantum = q; $('source').classList.toggle('quantum', q);
    $('sourceText').textContent = "Random errors: from your browser's generator.";
  }
  setSource(false);
  async function refill() {
    if (!SOURCE.ENDPOINT || fetching || pool.length > 8192) return;
    fetching = true;
    try { const r = await fetch(SOURCE.ENDPOINT + '?n=4096', { cache: 'no-store' }); const j = await r.json();
      if (!j.ok || !Array.isArray(j.values)) throw 0; pool.push(...j.values); if (!quantum) setSource(true); }
    catch (e) { if (quantum || !SOURCE.tried) setSource(false, true); }
    finally { SOURCE.tried = true; fetching = false; }
  }
  setInterval(refill, 1500); refill();
  const u32 = new Uint32Array(1);
  function uniform() {                         // strictly between 0 and 1, from 4 random bytes
    let x;
    if (quantum && pool.length >= 4) { const b = pool.splice(0, 4); x = ((b[0] << 24) >>> 0) + (b[1] << 16) + (b[2] << 8) + b[3]; }
    else x = crypto.getRandomValues(u32)[0];
    return (x + .5) / 4294967296;
  }
  let spare = null;
  function gauss() {                           // standard normal (Box–Muller)
    if (spare !== null) { const s = spare; spare = null; return s; }
    const r = Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(uniform())), a = 2 * Math.PI * uniform();
    spare = r * Math.sin(a); return r * Math.cos(a);
  }
  // Slowly wandering error (first-order Gauss–Markov), exact for any time step.
  class Wander {
    constructor(tau) { this.tau = tau; this.x = gauss(); this.y = gauss(); }
    step(dt) { const p = Math.exp(-dt / this.tau), q = Math.sqrt(1 - p * p); this.x = p * this.x + q * gauss(); this.y = p * this.y + q * gauss(); }
  }

  // ================= Physics constants =================
  const C = 299792458;
  const DRIFT = 38.6e-6 / 86400;               // net relativistic clock gain, seconds per second
  const ECC_K = 4.442807633e-10 * 5153.7;      // |F|·√A : eccentricity clock term in seconds per unit eccentricity (≈ 2.29 µs)
  const HALF_SIDEREAL = 43082;                 // GPS orbital period, seconds

  // ================= Modes =================
  const MODES = {
    phone: { badge: 'Phone GPS · open sky', cls: '',
      info: 'A phone or handheld under open sky, using the satellites alone. One fix a second.' },
    ppp: { badge: 'Free corrections · no base', cls: 'ppp',
      info: 'Precise Point Positioning: precise orbit and clock corrections arrive by satellite or internet (like Galileo\'s free High Accuracy Service). No base station, but it takes <b>about 5 minutes to converge</b>. Try 10×.' },
    rtk: { badge: 'RTK rover · fixed', cls: 'rtk',
      info: 'A survey rover getting corrections every second from a <b>base station</b> on a known point. The scale is now in <b>centimeters</b>.' },
    einstein: { badge: 'Einstein off · time-lapse', cls: 'off',
      info: 'The satellite clocks lose their relativity fix and gain 38 µs a day. Time-lapse: <b>1 second = 1 hour</b>, one fix per minute.' },
  };
  let mode = 'phone', speed = 1, baseline = 10000, clockSolve = true, running = true;

  // ================= Receiver state =================
  let t = 0, fixes = [], nFix = 0, sinceTrack = 0, acc = 0;
  let wA, wB, rtkFixAt, sats, P4, P3, eLast = null;
  const MAXF = 4000, WIN = 300;

  function newSky() {                          // 8 satellites, each with its own oval orbit
    sats = Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) => {
      const az = 2 * Math.PI * (i + uniform() * .8) / 8, el = (15 + uniform() * 70) * Math.PI / 180;
      return { u: [Math.cos(el) * Math.sin(az), Math.cos(el) * Math.cos(az), Math.sin(el)], e: .002 + uniform() * .018, ph: 2 * Math.PI * uniform() };
    });
    const G4 = sats.map(s => [-s.u[0], -s.u[1], -s.u[2], 1]), G3 = sats.map(s => [-s.u[0], -s.u[1], -s.u[2]]);
    P4 = pinv(G4); P3 = pinv(G3);
  }
  function pinv(G) {                           // (GᵀG)⁻¹Gᵀ by Gauss–Jordan
    const n = G[0].length, N = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => Array.from({ length: 2 * n }, (_, j) => j < n ? G.reduce((s, r) => s + r[i] * r[j], 0) : (j - n === i ? 1 : 0)));
    for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {
      let p = c; for (let r = c + 1; r < n; r++) if (Math.abs(N[r][c]) > Math.abs(N[p][c])) p = r; [N[c], N[p]] = [N[p], N[c]];
      const d = N[c][c]; for (let j = 0; j < 2 * n; j++) N[c][j] /= d;
      for (let r = 0; r < n; r++) if (r !== c) { const f = N[r][c]; for (let j = 0; j < 2 * n; j++) N[r][j] -= f * N[c][j]; }
    }
    const inv = N.map(r => r.slice(n));
    return inv.map(row => G.map(g => row.reduce((s, v, k) => s + v * g[k], 0)));
  }

  function resetAll() {
    t = 0; fixes = []; nFix = 0; acc = 0; eLast = null; spare = null;
    wA = new Wander(mode === 'rtk' ? 10 : mode === 'ppp' ? 30 : 60); wB = new Wander(4);
    rtkFixAt = 2 + uniform() * 6;              // RTK start-up: 2 to 8 seconds
    if (mode === 'einstein') newSky();
    zoom = targetZoom(); updatePanels();
  }

  // One position fix after dt seconds. Returns east/north error in metres.
  function fix(dt) {
    t += dt; wA.step(dt); wB.step(dt);
    if (mode === 'phone') return [1.9 * wA.x + .6 * gauss(), 1.9 * wA.y + .6 * gauss()];
    if (mode === 'ppp') {
      const s = .065 + .9 * Math.exp(-t / 75);  // per-axis σ shrinking as it converges
      return [s * (.9 * wA.x + .44 * gauss()), s * (.9 * wA.y + .44 * gauss())];
    }
    if (mode === 'rtk') {
      if (t < rtkFixAt) return [.25 * wB.x + .15 * gauss(), .25 * wB.y + .15 * gauss()];   // float, before the fix
      const s = (.008 + 1e-6 * baseline) / Math.SQRT2;                                        // 8 mm + 1 ppm RMS, per axis
      return [s * (.8 * wA.x + .6 * gauss()), s * (.8 * wA.y + .6 * gauss())];
    }
    // Einstein off: every satellite clock gains the same 38.6 µs/day, plus its own eccentricity wobble.
    const common = DRIFT * t;
    const eps = sats.map(s => -C * (common + ECC_K * s.e * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * t / HALF_SIDEREAL + s.ph)));
    const P = clockSolve ? P4 : P3;
    const d = P.map(row => row.reduce((acc2, v, i) => acc2 + v * eps[i], 0));
    eLast = { common, east: d[0], north: d[1], up: d[2], clock: clockSolve ? d[3] / C : 0, range: C * common };
    return [d[0] + 1.9 * wA.x + .6 * gauss(), d[1] + 1.9 * wA.y + .6 * gauss()];
  }

  // ================= Stats =================
  function radii() { const r = []; for (let i = Math.max(0, fixes.length - WIN); i < fixes.length; i++) r.push(Math.hypot(fixes[i][0], fixes[i][1])); return r.sort((a, b) => a - b); }
  const q = (s, p) => s.length ? s[Math.min(s.length - 1, Math.floor(p * s.length))] : 0;

  // ================= Units =================
  function len(m) {
    const a = Math.abs(m);
    if (a < .1) return `${(a * 100).toFixed(1)} cm <small>${(a / .0254).toFixed(1)} in</small>`;
    if (a < 1000) return `${a < 10 ? a.toFixed(2) : a.toFixed(1)} m <small>${(a / .3048).toFixed(a < 10 ? 1 : 0)} ft</small>`;
    return `${(a / 1000).toFixed(a < 100000 ? 2 : 0)} km <small>${(a / 1609.344).toFixed(1)} mi</small>`;
  }
  const plain = m => len(m).replace(/ <small>(.*)<\/small>/, ' ($1)');
  function clock(s) { s = Math.floor(s); const h = Math.floor(s / 3600), m = Math.floor(s / 60) % 60, x = s % 60; return h ? `${h}:${String(m).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(x).padStart(2, '0')}` : `${m}:${String(x).padStart(2, '0')}`; }

  // ================= Map =================
  const cv = $('map'), ctx = cv.getContext('2d');
  let W = 0, H = 0, R = 0, cx = 0, cy = 0, topo = null, zoom = 8;
  function size() {
    const r = cv.getBoundingClientRect(), dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;
    cv.width = r.width * dpr; cv.height = r.height * dpr; ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    W = r.width; H = r.height; cx = W / 2; cy = H / 2 + 8; R = Math.min(W, H) / 2 - 34;
    topo = document.createElement('canvas'); topo.width = cv.width; topo.height = cv.height;
    const g = topo.getContext('2d'); g.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    g.fillStyle = '#0A1510'; g.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
    const hills = [[W * .18, H * .22, 1], [W * .82, H * .7, 1.2], [W * .7, H * .12, .7]];
    g.lineWidth = 1;
    for (const [hx, hy, k] of hills) for (let i = 1; i < 16; i++) {
      g.strokeStyle = i % 5 ? 'rgba(126,170,120,.10)' : 'rgba(126,170,120,.2)';
      g.beginPath();
      for (let a = 0; a <= 64; a++) {
        const th = a / 64 * 2 * Math.PI, rr = i * 26 * k * (1 + .18 * Math.sin(3 * th + i * .4) + .1 * Math.cos(5 * th - i * .3));
        const x = hx + rr * Math.cos(th), y = hy + rr * .8 * Math.sin(th); a ? g.lineTo(x, y) : g.moveTo(x, y);
      }
      g.stroke();
    }
  }
  addEventListener('resize', size); size();

  function niceStep(span) { const raw = span / 3, p = Math.pow(10, Math.floor(Math.log10(raw))), f = raw / p; return (f < 1.5 ? 1 : f < 3.5 ? 2 : 5) * p; }
  function ringLabel(m) { if (m < 1) return `${+(m * 100).toPrecision(3)} cm`; if (m < 1000) return `${+m.toPrecision(3)} m`; return `${+(m / 1000).toPrecision(3)} km`; }
  function targetZoom() {
    const floor = { phone: 6, ppp: .4, rtk: mode === 'rtk' && t < rtkFixAt ? .8 : .03 + 2e-6 * baseline, einstein: 6 }[mode];
    const r = radii(); return Math.max(floor, q(r, .99) * 1.25, fixes.length ? Math.hypot(...fixes[fixes.length - 1]) * 1.15 : 0);
  }

  function drawMarker(x, y) {
    const g = ctx.createRadialGradient(x - 4, y - 4, 2, x, y, 17);
    g.addColorStop(0, '#FFE9A8'); g.addColorStop(.55, '#D9A93A'); g.addColorStop(1, '#8A6418');
    ctx.fillStyle = g; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 16, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = '#5E430D'; ctx.lineWidth = 1.5; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 12, 0, 7); ctx.stroke();
    ctx.strokeStyle = '#3E2C06'; ctx.lineWidth = 1.6; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x - 6, y); ctx.lineTo(x + 6, y); ctx.moveTo(x, y - 6); ctx.lineTo(x, y + 6); ctx.stroke();
  }

  function draw() {
    ctx.drawImage(topo, 0, 0, W, H);
    const pxm = R / zoom, step = niceStep(zoom);
    // rings
    ctx.font = '600 13px "IBM Plex Mono", monospace'; ctx.textBaseline = 'middle'; ctx.textAlign = 'left';
    for (let k = 1; k * step <= zoom * 1.4; k++) {
      const rr = k * step * pxm;
      ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(188,203,191,.2)'; ctx.lineWidth = 1; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(cx, cy, rr, 0, 7); ctx.stroke();
      if (cy - rr > 56) { ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(188,203,191,.7)'; ctx.fillText(ringLabel(k * step), cx + 6, cy - rr - 8); }
    }
    ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(188,203,191,.12)'; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(cx - R * 1.3, cy); ctx.lineTo(cx + R * 1.3, cy); ctx.moveTo(cx, cy - R * 1.3); ctx.lineTo(cx, cy + R * 1.3); ctx.stroke();

    // 95% circle
    const r = radii();
    if (r.length > 20) {
      const r95 = q(r, .95) * pxm;
      ctx.setLineDash([7, 6]); ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255,122,46,.75)'; ctx.lineWidth = 2; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(cx, cy, r95, 0, 7); ctx.stroke(); ctx.setLineDash([]);
      ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(255,122,46,.9)'; ctx.font = '700 12px "IBM Plex Sans Condensed", sans-serif'; ctx.textAlign = 'center';
      if (cy + r95 + 16 < H - 8) ctx.fillText('95% OF FIXES', cx, cy + r95 + 14);
      ctx.textAlign = 'left';
    }

    drawMarker(cx, cy);

    // fixes: older ones fade out
    const col = mode === 'rtk' ? '91,240,166' : mode === 'ppp' ? '127,212,255' : mode === 'einstein' ? '255,111,134' : '255,122,46';
    const n = Math.min(fixes.length, 900), start = fixes.length - n;
    for (let i = start; i < fixes.length; i++) {
      const [x, y] = fixes[i], a = .12 + .6 * (i - start) / n;
      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${col},${a})`; ctx.fillRect(cx + x * pxm - 1.5, cy - y * pxm - 1.5, 3, 3);
    }
    if (fixes.length) {
      const [x, y] = fixes[fixes.length - 1], px = cx + x * pxm, py = cy - y * pxm;
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${col},.5)`; ctx.lineWidth = 1.5; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(cx, cy); ctx.lineTo(px, py); ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${col},.25)`; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(px, py, 13, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillStyle = '#fff'; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(px, py, 5.5, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillStyle = `rgb(${col})`; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(px, py, 3.5, 0, 7); ctx.fill();
    }

    // north arrow and scale bar
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(239,244,236,.8)'; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(W - 30, 22); ctx.lineTo(W - 38, 44); ctx.lineTo(W - 30, 39); ctx.lineTo(W - 22, 44); ctx.closePath(); ctx.fill();
    ctx.font = '700 13px "IBM Plex Sans Condensed", sans-serif'; ctx.textAlign = 'center'; ctx.fillText('N', W - 30, 56);
    const sb = step * pxm; ctx.textAlign = 'left';
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(239,244,236,.85)'; ctx.fillRect(16, H - 26, sb, 4); ctx.fillRect(16, H - 32, 2, 16); ctx.fillRect(16 + sb - 2, H - 32, 2, 16);
    ctx.font = '600 13px "IBM Plex Mono", monospace'; ctx.fillText(ringLabel(step), 24 + sb, H - 24);
    if (mode === 'einstein') { ctx.textAlign = 'right'; ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(255,111,134,.95)'; ctx.font = '600 14px "IBM Plex Mono", monospace'; ctx.fillText(`Day ${(t / 86400).toFixed(2)}`, W - 16, H - 24); }
    ctx.textAlign = 'left';
  }

  // ================= Panels =================
  function updatePanels() {
    const m = MODES[mode];
    $('modeInfo').innerHTML = m.info;
    const b = $('badge'); b.className = 'badge ' + m.cls;
    b.textContent = mode === 'rtk' ? (t < rtkFixAt ? 'RTK rover · float, finding the fix…' : 'RTK rover · fixed') : mode === 'ppp' ? (t < 300 ? 'Free corrections · converging…' : 'Free corrections · converged') : m.badge;
    $('speedCtl').classList.toggle('hide', mode === 'einstein');
    $('baseCtl').classList.toggle('hide', mode !== 'rtk');
    $('clockCtl').classList.toggle('hide', mode !== 'einstein');
    $('einPanel').classList.toggle('hide', mode !== 'einstein');

    const r = radii(), last = fixes[fixes.length - 1];
    $('nowErr').innerHTML = last ? len(Math.hypot(last[0], last[1])) : '–';
    $('r50').innerHTML = r.length > 10 ? len(q(r, .5)) : '–';
    $('r95').innerHTML = r.length > 20 ? len(q(r, .95)) : '–';
    $('nFix').textContent = nFix.toLocaleString('en-US');
    $('simT').textContent = mode === 'einstein' ? `${(t / 86400).toFixed(2)} days` : clock(t);
    const rms = .008 + 1e-6 * baseline;
    $('spec').innerHTML = {
      phone: 'GPS.gov: smartphones are typically within <b>4.9 m</b> (16 ft) under open sky. Stats are for the last 300 fixes.',
      ppp: 'Galileo HAS target: within <b>20 cm</b> (95%) after about 5 minutes. Commercial services converge faster.',
      rtk: `Typical spec: <b>8 mm + 1 ppm</b> RMS horizontal. At ${baseline / 1000} km that's <b>${(rms * 1000).toFixed(0)} mm</b> RMS, about <b>${(rms / Math.SQRT2 * 2.448 * 1000).toFixed(0)} mm</b> for 95%.`,
      einstein: 'Stats are for the last 300 fixes (5 hours).',
    }[mode];

    if (mode === 'einstein' && eLast) {
      $('eGain').innerHTML = `${(eLast.common * 1e6).toFixed(1)} µs`;
      $('eRange').innerHTML = len(eLast.range);
      $('ePos').innerHTML = len(Math.hypot(last[0], last[1]));
      $('eClock').innerHTML = clockSolve ? `${Math.abs(eLast.clock * 1e6).toFixed(1)} µs` : '0 (assumed perfect)';
      $('eNote').innerHTML = clockSolve
        ? 'The shared gain goes into the receiver\'s clock, not your position. What\'s left is each satellite\'s own <b>eccentricity wobble</b> (up to ±15 m of range) on top of the usual noise.'
        : `With no clock to absorb it, the short ranges push you toward the satellites: <b>${plain(eLast.up)}</b> up in the air, ${plain(Math.hypot(last[0], last[1]))} sideways.`;
    }
    verdict(r, last);
  }

  function verdict(r, last) {
    const v = $('verdict'); v.classList.toggle('off', mode === 'einstein');
    if (r.length < 20) { v.textContent = mode === 'einstein' ? 'The satellite clocks just lost their relativity fix…' : 'Collecting the first position fixes…'; return; }
    const r95 = q(r, .95);
    if (mode === 'phone') v.innerHTML = `95% of fixes are within <b>${plain(r95)}</b> of the marker. Watch how the dot <b>wanders</b> rather than jumps: the errors change slowly, over a minute or more. That's why averaging for a few seconds barely helps, and why surveyors need corrections.`;
    else if (mode === 'ppp') v.innerHTML = t < 300
      ? `Converging: ${clock(t)} in. The receiver is still working out the atmosphere and its own biases. 95% of recent fixes are within <b>${plain(r95)}</b>.`
      : `Converged. 95% of recent fixes are within <b>${plain(r95)}</b>, with no base station anywhere. But it took minutes to get here, and RTK gets there in seconds.`;
    else if (mode === 'rtk') v.innerHTML = t < rtkFixAt
      ? 'Float solution: the rover is still counting whole radio waves. Decimeters, not centimeters, until it locks…'
      : `Fixed. 95% of fixes are within <b>${plain(r95)}</b> of the marker, ${baseline / 1000} km from the base station. Try 30 km: each extra kilometer adds about a millimeter.`;
    else if (clockSolve) v.innerHTML = `Day ${(t / 86400).toFixed(1)}: every satellite clock is <b>${(eLast.common * 1e6).toFixed(0)} µs</b> fast, so every range is <b>${plain(eLast.range)}</b> too short. Yet you're only <b>${plain(Math.hypot(last[0], last[1]))}</b> off, because your receiver puts the shared error in its own clock. What really broke is <b>the time</b>: it's now ${Math.abs(eLast.clock * 1e6).toFixed(0)} µs wrong.`;
    else v.innerHTML = `The myth, playing out: a receiver that trusts the satellites' clocks is now <b>${plain(Math.hypot(last[0], last[1]))}</b> off sideways, and <b>${plain(eLast.up)}</b> up in the air. No real receiver works this way, because none has a perfect clock.`;
  }

  // ================= Loop =================
  let lastT = performance.now(), lastPanel = 0;
  function frame(now) {
    const dt = Math.min(.1, (now - lastT) / 1000); lastT = now;
    if (running) {
      const perSec = mode === 'einstein' ? 60 : speed, step = mode === 'einstein' ? 60 : 1;
      acc += dt * perSec;
      while (acc >= 1) { acc--; fixes.push(fix(step)); nFix++; sinceTrack++; }
      if (fixes.length > MAXF) fixes.splice(0, fixes.length - MAXF);
      if (sinceTrack >= 100) { sinceTrack = 0; }
    }
    zoom += (targetZoom() - zoom) * Math.min(1, dt * 2.5);
    draw();
    if (now - lastPanel > 250) { lastPanel = now; updatePanels(); }
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // ================= Controls =================
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-m]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
    mode = b.dataset.m; document.querySelectorAll('[data-m]').forEach(x => x.classList.toggle('on', x === b)); resetAll();
  }));
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-s]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
    speed = +b.dataset.s; document.querySelectorAll('[data-s]').forEach(x => x.classList.toggle('on', x === b));
  }));
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-d]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
    baseline = +b.dataset.d; document.querySelectorAll('[data-d]').forEach(x => x.classList.toggle('on', x === b)); resetAll();
  }));
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-c]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
    clockSolve = b.dataset.c === '1'; document.querySelectorAll('[data-c]').forEach(x => x.classList.toggle('on', x === b)); resetAll();
  }));
  $('run').addEventListener('click', () => { running = !running; $('run').textContent = running ? 'Pause' : 'Run'; });
  $('reset').addEventListener('click', resetAll);

  resetAll(); requestAnimationFrame(frame);
})();
</script>
<script>
// AugieLab shared "What's happening?" button.
// Add <template id="explain"> ...headings and paragraphs... </template> to a page, then load this script.
// Optional: <body data-explain-bottom="40"> to lift the button, data-explain-autohide to hide it when the mouse is idle.
(() => {
  const tpl = document.getElementById('explain');
  if (!tpl) return;
  const bottom = (document.body.dataset.explainBottom || 16) + 'px';
  const css = `
    .lab-why { position: fixed; left: 16px; bottom: ${bottom}; z-index: 40; padding: .7rem 1.15rem; border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer;
      font: 600 16px/1.2 "IBM Plex Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; color: #fff; background: rgba(12,16,24,.82);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.35); box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.45); transition: opacity .6s; }
    .lab-why:hover { border-color: #fff; }
    .lab-why:focus-visible, .lab-x:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #FFD36E; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .lab-why.idle { opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
    .lab-info { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 41; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 18px;
      background: rgba(5,8,12,.8); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: opacity .3s; }
    .lab-info.open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }
    .lab-box { position: relative; width: min(660px, 100%); max-height: 88vh; overflow-y: auto; background: #1C2230; color: #E9EDF4;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.22); border-radius: 10px; padding: 2rem 1.7rem 1.6rem; font: 18px/1.6 "IBM Plex Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; }
    .lab-box h2 { font: 700 1.6em/1.2 "IBM Plex Sans Condensed", "IBM Plex Sans", sans-serif; margin: 0 0 .5em; padding-right: 3rem; }
    .lab-box h3 { font-size: 1.02em; color: #FFD36E; margin: 1.1em 0 .25em; }
    .lab-box p { margin: 0; color: #D5DCE7; }
    .lab-x { position: absolute; top: 12px; right: 12px; width: 46px; height: 46px; border-radius: 50%; cursor: pointer;
      font-size: 26px; line-height: 1; color: #fff; background: rgba(255,255,255,.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3); }`;
  const st = document.createElement('style'); st.textContent = css; document.head.appendChild(st);

  const btn = document.createElement('button'); btn.className = 'lab-why'; btn.type = 'button'; btn.setAttribute('aria-haspopup', 'dialog'); btn.textContent = "✦ What's happening?";
  const wrap = document.createElement('div'); wrap.className = 'lab-info'; wrap.setAttribute('role', 'dialog'); wrap.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
  const box = document.createElement('div'); box.className = 'lab-box'; box.appendChild(tpl.content.cloneNode(true));
  const x = document.createElement('button'); x.className = 'lab-x'; x.type = 'button'; x.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Close'); x.textContent = '×';
  box.prepend(x); wrap.appendChild(box); document.body.append(btn, wrap);

  const open = () => { wrap.classList.add('open'); x.focus(); };
  const close = () => { wrap.classList.remove('open'); btn.focus(); };
  btn.addEventListener('click', open); x.addEventListener('click', close);
  wrap.addEventListener('click', e => { if (e.target === wrap) close(); });
  addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.key === 'Escape' && wrap.classList.contains('open')) { e.stopPropagation(); close(); } }, true);

  if ('explainAutohide' in document.body.dataset) {
    let t; const wake = () => { btn.classList.remove('idle'); clearTimeout(t); t = setTimeout(() => btn.classList.add('idle'), 5000); };
    addEventListener('mousemove', wake); wake();
  }
})();
</script>
</body>
